# Tests, coverage, and RuboCop

After changing application code, keep the suite green and the quality bar intact.

## Coverage

Ruby SimpleCov must stay at **100%** for models, serializers, controllers, mailers, helpers, and `lib/`.

Vitest must stay at **100%** for `app/frontend/lib` and `app/frontend/i18n.ts`.

New behavior needs tests in the same change. Do not merge or finish with uncovered branches.

## Home sections

Public home specs must cover every section, including the empty/hidden case:

hero, skills, experience, featured projects, about, certifications, education, contact.

Use Inertia matchers (`render_component`, `have_props`, `have_flash`), not `inertia.component` / `inertia.props`. After POST/PATCH/DELETE with redirect, call `follow_redirect!` before asserting flash or props.

## RuboCop

Run `bin/rubocop` on Ruby changes and leave the code organized. Do not disable cops to hide a mess; match existing Omakase style.

## Commands

```bash
bin/rspec
bin/rubocop
npm run test
```
